---
description: Test conventions (workflow tests vs. service/hook tests, RTL query priority, no snapshots, MSW-backed)
globs: "src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

Full rule: see `AGENTS.md` § Testing.

- Workflow-over-unit-testing: no standalone test for a `src/components/common/` primitive —
  it gets coverage transitively through the feature workflows that use it.
- A feature component → `<Name>.workflow.test.tsx`, co-located in the feature folder (see
  `ExampleWidget.workflow.test.tsx`). A `src/services/`/`src/hooks/` file (reusable logic) →
  standalone `*.test.ts`, co-located next to it.
- Use `renderWithProviders` from `src/test/renderWithProviders.tsx` for anything touching
  TanStack Query or react-router context.
- Query like a user: `getByRole`, `getByLabelText`, not `getByTestId`. **No snapshots.**
- Drive the real MSW-backed network layer (`src/mocks/handlers.ts`, `server.use(...)` for a
  one-off override) — never an inline mock of `apiClient`/`fetch`.
- Prefer `findBy*` for async (MSW-backed) data. A hook with a timer uses
  `vi.useFakeTimers()` + `vi.advanceTimersByTime(...)`, never a real `setTimeout` wait.
